{"summary":"Accepted amendments identify a real legacy-metadata migration bug, missing provenance on load-bearing kinetics/constants, and a concrete unit-safety problem. Rejected amendments either overread the bead’s representative-coverage requirement, duplicate provenance warnings already carried in the authoritative data/docs, or conflate the separate alkalinity worktree with the provenance bead.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-92da51e1","decision":"accept","rationale":"`legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l()` rescales the numeric parameter, but `move_legacy_process_param_meta_key()` only renames the metadata entry. That leaves legacy `unit` strings and any `valid_range` bounds attached unchanged to a concentration-valued field, so migrated metadata can become semantically wrong and produce misleading display or range warnings."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-c9b5f0d8","decision":"reject","rationale":"The bead requires representative enriched coverage for the targeted chemistry/ecology/shrimp families, not per-parameter metadata in every plant, substrate, and source-water preset. That representative coverage already exists through `process/default.toml`, the annotated source-water presets, the substrate `colonizable_area_factor` entries, and `shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml`, with the remaining files explicitly documented as follow-up work."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-1a29bd8c","decision":"reject","rationale":"`low_temp_repro_ramp_width_c` is already marked `placeholder` in the authoritative provenance locations: the shrimp TOML metadata and `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md`. Adding a use-site TODO in `shrimp.rs` would duplicate provenance text without changing validation, runtime behavior, or any user-facing warning path."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-f497e356","decision":"accept","rationale":"These nitrifier and decomposer rate, yield, and decay coefficients materially control cycling speed and biomass turnover, yet they have no per-parameter confidence metadata and are not surfaced in the provenance summary. That leaves major calibration knobs indistinguishable from literature anchors, which is a real maintainability and tuning problem."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-7fd25e44","decision":"accept","rationale":"`ATMOSPHERIC_CO2_PPM` feeds every Henry-law equilibrium calculation, but unlike the neighboring carbonate constants it has no source or fixed-ambient-scope note in code and is absent from the provenance summary table. A short provenance comment is warranted for scientific traceability and maintainability."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-2eb078b6","decision":"reject","rationale":"The cited diff is plainly the separate `tanksim-6e5.4.7` alkalinity worktree, and its changes align with that bead by adding named alkalinity constants, budget/tracing plumbing, and nitrification tests. Treating that as a failed `tanksim-6e5.7.2` implementation is a task-tracking mixup rather than a defect in the patch itself."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-7fcbfd69","decision":"accept","rationale":"The new alkalinity path stores meq values in APIs and fields named `in_mg`/`out_mg`/`net_mg`, and some helper/assertion output still labels those values as `mg`. That is a real unit-safety and maintainability defect because future callers can mix mg and meq semantics without the type surface catching it."}]}